# Flutter AI Agent Framework Repository Rules

This repository packages agent assets; it is not a Flutter application. Do not require a target project's `pubspec.yaml` or `.agents/context/` files to maintain this framework.

When changing a skill, read its `SKILL.md`, `metadata.yaml`, and referenced local resources first. Keep the frontmatter name equal to the folder name, keep descriptions precise about capability and trigger context, and preserve progressive disclosure.

When changing project initialization or Antigravity compatibility, treat `.agents/` as the only new-install root. Keep skills in `.agents/skills/`, workspace rules in `.agents/rules/`, framework policies in `.agents/governance/`, project state in `.agents/context/`, and verification utilities in `.agents/tools/`. Retain `.agent/` only inside the explicit legacy migration path; never write new project assets there.

Update the initializer, validation contracts, documentation, and Windows smoke tests together when a project path changes. Before finalizing, run `python3 tools/validate_framework.py` and report platform-specific behavior that has not been executed.
